One thing I particularly like about this example is that it demonstrates a pattern your medical example didn't: an observation can weaken one hypothesis while simultaneously suggesting a new, more specific one.

Here, O4["update_date is updated"] weakens H2 as originally conceived ("cache invalidation isn't happening"), while O3 leads naturally to the refined hypothesis H3 ("the invalidation exists, but there's a race"). That's a nice illustration of investigations becoming more precise rather than simply eliminating possibilities.


